# Mean and standard error: mean_se

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

This notebook follows the examples on ggplot2's reference page for
[`mean_se()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/mean_se.html), in the order the page gives
them. Each example shows ggplot2's code first and then Giggly's. An example Giggly cannot draw
yet keeps its ggplot2 code and names what it is waiting for, so the page is also a list of what
remains.

`mean_se()` takes a numeric vector and returns a data frame of one row: the mean in `y`, and the
mean minus and plus a multiple of the standard error, one by default, in `ymin` and `ymax`. It is
made for `stat_summary()`. Not in Giggly yet: `mean_se()` and `stat_summary()`.

## The mean of random values

```r
set.seed(1)
x <- rnorm(100)
mean_se(x)
```

With `set.seed(1)` fixing R's random numbers, `rnorm(100)` draws 100 values from a standard
normal distribution, and `mean_se()` returns their mean and the mean one standard error either
side. Not in Giggly yet: `mean_se()`.
